/* renderer — a tiny folk-tale markup engine, and a Judge stress test.

   Blocks are a closed union of object types; inline runs are a mixed
   union of text and two object types. Every dispatch is a Judge:
   exhaustive arms with no Otherwise, a grouped arm that must re-narrow
   inside, an expression subject, and returns that live only in arms. */

Define object heading with (the text title, the number level).
Define object paragraph with (the catalogue of (text or emphasis or link) body).
Define object quote with (the catalogue of (text or emphasis or link) body, the text source).
Define object code-block with (the text content).
Define object emphasis with (the text span).
Define object link with (the text label, the text target).

Bind text to render-inline, given (the (text or emphasis or link) piece):
    Judge piece, where it is:
        A text, return it.
        An emphasis, return "*{it's span}*".
        A link, return "{it's label} ({it's target})".
    Done.
Done.

Bind text to render-body, given (the catalogue of (text or emphasis or link) body):
    Define out as "".
    For each piece in body, repeat:
        The out becomes "{out} {cast render-inline on (piece)}".
    Done.
    Return out.
Done.

Bind text to render-block, given (the (heading or paragraph or quote or code-block) block):
    Judge block, where it is:
        A heading:
            Define marks as "".
            Define i as 1.
            While i is not greater than it's level, repeat:
                The marks becomes "{marks}#".
                The i becomes i + 1.
            Done.
            Return "{marks} {it's title}".
        Done.
        A quote or a paragraph:
            If it is a quote, return "> {cast render-body on (it's body)} — {it's source}".
            Otherwise, return "{cast render-body on (it's body)}".
        Done.
        A code-block, return "```\n{it's content}\n```".
    Done.
Done.

Bind void to play:
    Define doc as a catalogue of (heading or paragraph or quote or code-block) with (
        A new heading { the title "How Rabbit Brought Fire", the level 1 },
        A new paragraph { the body a catalogue of (text or emphasis or link) with (
            "In the beginning the people had no fire, and the ",
            A new emphasis { the span "Weasels" },
            " kept it for themselves.") },
        A new quote { the body a catalogue of (text or emphasis or link) with (
            "I can run and swim faster than the Weasels, and I am also a ",
            A new emphasis { the span "good dancer" },
            ".") , the source "Rabbit, to the council" },
        A new code-block { the content "Seed the chance with 42." },
        A new paragraph { the body a catalogue of (text or emphasis or link) with (
            "So he danced close to the fire until the pine tar in his hair caught, and ran ",
            A new link { the label "home", the target "the hollow tree" },
            " with his head ablaze.") }).

    For each block in doc, repeat:
        State cast render-block on (block).
        State "".
    Done.

    Judge the first of doc, where it is:
        A heading, State "the document opens with: {it's title}".
        Otherwise, State "the document opens with body text".
    Done.
Done.

Cast play.